ALVA — Complete Controller System Update

Ergonomic Character-Specific Controls, Controller Detection, Menu Navigation, and Full Customization

OBJECTIVE

Implement a complete, high-quality controller system for the ALVA game.

Repository: hiyroscript/alva

This update must introduce reliable PlayStation and Xbox controller support, controller connection management, a custom circular menu cursor, carefully designed default controls for every playable character, and a comprehensive per-character controller customization system.

The update must integrate cleanly with ALVA’s existing architecture, preserve the current gameplay mechanics, and support future characters.

MOST IMPORTANT REQUIREMENT: COMFORTABLE CONTROLS ARE THE HIGHEST PRIORITY.

The purpose of this update is not simply to make controller buttons activate abilities. The purpose is to make ALVA genuinely comfortable, intuitive, responsive, and enjoyable to play on a controller.

Every default control must be chosen according to how natural and comfortable the action is to execute.

ALVA has a unique character system. Each fighter has different moves, abilities, and mechanics. Therefore, controller layouts must respect those differences.

This is the central design philosophy:

Universal gameplay actions have consistent recommended defaults across all characters. Character-specific actions receive their own ergonomically optimized defaults. Players can then fully customize either category for each individual character.

This principle must guide the entire implementation.

