7.1 Movement

Use the left joystick for normal character movement.

Horizontal stick direction determines left/right movement.

Preserve ALVA’s existing movement behavior.

Do not alter acceleration, momentum, jump physics, air movement, or running speed.

7.2 Jump

Cross/A is the universal default Jump button.

This should remain consistent because Jump is one of the most frequent and important gameplay actions.

Preserve:

* Normal jumping.
* Higher jumps based on hold duration.
* Air jumping.
* Triple jumping.
* Existing jump buffering.

7.3 Dash and air dash

L1/LB is the universal default Dash button.

This is particularly important.

The player should be able to Dash without moving their right thumb away from the attack buttons.

The direction depends on the left joystick.

Examples:

Left joystick right + L1 = Dash right.

Left joystick left + L1 = Dash left.

Neutral joystick + L1 = Dash in the current facing direction.

Use the existing ALVA Dash and air-dash mechanics.

Do not change their movement values or Energy costs.

A held Dash button must not repeatedly trigger Dashes.

A fresh valid activation must issue one Dash request, using the intended direction at activation.

Preserve the existing internal mouvementLeftPressed and mouvementRightPressed fields.

7.4 Shield

Circle/B is the universal default defensive button.

Shield must be held.

Holding Circle/B on the ground raises Shield.

Releasing it lowers Shield.

Never make Shield automatically toggle on and off.

Preserve:

* Shield startup.
* Shield release.
* Perfect Shield.
* Shield Energy.
* Blocking behavior.
* Recovery and restrictions.

7.5 Deflect

In the air, a fresh Circle/B press triggers Deflect where supported.

Deflect is a press-based action.

Holding Circle/B must not repeatedly activate it.

Do not introduce aerial shielding or air dodging.

