14.2 New character defaults

When a new playable character is introduced:

1. Identify its universal actions.
2. Identify every unique ability.
3. Understand how each ability works.
4. Determine whether it is grounded, aerial, directional, held, or context-sensitive.
5. Choose comfortable default controller bindings.
6. Ensure no unintended conflicts.
7. Make all actions available for customization.
8. Add brief ability descriptions.
9. Validate the character’s controller profile.

A new fighter should receive a safe, editable fallback when no individually authored recommended defaults exist.

However, do not mistake the fallback for a finalized ergonomic control layout.

New fighters should receive consciously designed default bindings.

Important

The shared input engine must not contain hardcoded checks for specific character IDs.

Character-specific layout data may reference individual fighter IDs, but the controller engine itself must remain generic.

